# The Zig toolchain of the Ghostty build: an official upstream tarball pinned by URL and sha256 (Fedora packages only zig 0.16, Ghostty 1.4.0 needs
# 0.17: build.zig.zon .minimum_zig_version = "0.17.0"; Ghostty's build accepts the same major.minor with any patch >= the minimum). Parsed, never sourced.
# fetch-zig.sh checks size and sha256, compares the sha256 with ziglang.org/download/index.json at build time, and verifies the minisign signature when
# `minisign` is installed (the Containerfile installs it). A mismatch fails the Ghostty component build, which then degrades (it is optional).
# 0.17.0, not 0.17.1: Ghostty 1.4.0 was built against 0.17.0, and with 0.17.1 every zig build attempt failed in CI (a panic with --system, a hash mismatch
# for every dependency without it). ZIG_SIZE is not pinned (the size must equal the one index.json lists). Moved by the weekly check (the Zig minor follows from the Ghostty tag; a newer patch of the pinned minor is a separate low-priority pull request).
ZIG_VERSION=0.17.0
ZIG_URL=https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.0/zig-x86_64-linux-0.17.0.tar.xz
ZIG_SHA256=1cbe9df9f27e6b78d14ccbca43b6703a404ef79ef1c463de901d7f088d4e2026
ZIG_SIGNATURE_URL=https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.0/zig-x86_64-linux-0.17.0.tar.xz.minisig
ZIG_MINISIGN_KEY=RWSGOq2NVecA2UPNdBUZykf1CCb147pkmdtYxgb3Ti+JO/wCYvhbAb/U
